// The Windows application icon.
//
// Windows takes an executable's icon from its resources rather than from a
// file beside it, so unlike every other asset this port ships, the icon has to
// be compiled *in*. This is the whole resource script: one line that matters,
// and CMake configures the path into it because a .rc resolves relative names
// against wherever the resource compiler happened to be run from.
//
// The first icon in the table, by name order, is the one Explorer and the
// taskbar use -- hence the conventional IDI_ICON1, which sorts first and is
// what every other Windows program calls it too. The .ico itself carries every
// size from 16 to 256 (scripts/mkicon.py); Windows picks whichever it wants.
IDI_ICON1 ICON "@BB_ICON_ICO@"
